* win_det / dffr_lv setup-margin probe body (issue #189, the supervisor half
* of the #145/#148 ss diagnosis). Deck = design/netlist/supervisor.spice (the
* committed export; win_det and its siblings used verbatim) + this body.
* Not a design.
* The no-fault phase of the committed smoke stimulus (decks/sup_body.spice,
* d = 0.8 T) puts the TAPH falling edge 100 ps (50 % crossings of VDD) before
* the SECOND REF rising edge; the tt record captures low there and the ss probe
* (results/20261115T185844Z-probe/) mis-latches high. This probe sweeps that
* lead: REF is the smoke bench's own clock (Vck: 0.5 ns base delay, 30 ps
* edges, 1 ns period, vdd-scaled); TAPN is the unchanged 0.8 T copy; TAPH is
* ONE pulse whose fall 50 % point sits `lead` ps before the second REF rise,
* shaped (30 ps linear edges, the smoke slew) from the Vlead DC source
* (V = lead in ns: 0.100 V = 100 ps, the no-fault lead; lead < 0 means TAPH
* falls after the sampling edge, which must capture high at any corner).
* `lead` is swept across units through corners.supply_v (an alter of the Vlead
* source; the harness ic axis), NOT corners.params (the fleet runner image can
* lag the client -- sim/harness/gridspec.py).
* The sampler is the committed win_det itself with its supervisor-internal
* loads (REF drives XIREF + three dffr_lv CK inputs; TAPH drives XBUP.D), and
* `over` carries the XIPO inv_lv load it sees inside supervisor, so the load
* is the smoke bench's own. b_up is scored settled (at 2.4 ns, after the same
* clock edge, before the next) against 50 % of the corner's own rail (v(half)),
* so the same request grades every corner. The crossing times of the actual
* pins (t_ref_r2, t_taph_f) are recorded too, so every unit's true lead is
* read from the run, never assumed from the source parameter. Results are
* simulated, never measured.
Vdd vdd 0 1.2
Vck ck 0 PULSE(0 1 0.5n 30p 30p 0.47n 1n)
Vtn tn 0 PULSE(0 1 1.3n 30p 30p 0.47n 1n)
Vlead lead 0 DC 0.100
Bref ref 0 V = v(vdd)*v(ck)
Btapn tapn 0 V = v(vdd)*v(tn)
Btaph taph 0 V = v(vdd)*(((uramp(time-0.885e-9)/30e-12)-(uramp(uramp(time-0.885e-9)/30e-12-1)))-((uramp(time-1.500e-9+v(lead)*1e-9)/30e-12)-(uramp(uramp(time-1.500e-9+v(lead)*1e-9)/30e-12-1))))
Bhalf half 0 V = 0.5*v(vdd)
XWIN ref tapn taph over vdd 0 win_det
XLO over over_ld vdd 0 inv_lv
